VFBscDdoaVE4NjVraXFiTldlVDM5UlhJcTBuVjZhdlhWcjYtNWNBWjN0X01xQ29ScXVLN05oa2pMbTZ2aGxwY3d1TGhmSHM4ZHkwNGJUNUh4dEhmblhFeVkzNA?oc=5","date":"2026-11-03","zh":"英國人湧入後澳洲尋求改變與英國的簽證協議"}],"themes":[{"name":"訂單/合約","count":5},{"name":"財報","count":3},{"name":"AI 人工智慧","count":1},{"name":"加密貨幣","count":1},{"name":"併購","count":1}],"biz":{"tenk":{"form":"10-K","date":"2026-11-05","period":"2026-09-30","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1403161/000140316126000134/v-20260930.htm"},"overview":[{"en":"Visa is one of the world's leaders in digital payments. Our purpose is to uplift everyone, everywhere by being the best way to pay and be paid. Since Visa's early days in 1958, we have been in the business of facilitating secure, reliable and efficient global commerce and money movement. We provide transaction processing services (primarily authorization, clearing and settlement) among consumers, issuing and acquiring financial institutions and sellers in a structure we call the \"four-party\" model. Please see Four-Party Model discussion below.","zh":null},{"en":"As the payments ecosystem continues to evolve, we have broadened this model to include digital banks, digital wallets, a range of financial technology companies (fintechs), governments and non-governmental organizations (NGOs). We are focused on extending, enhancing and investing in our proprietary advanced transaction processing network, VisaNet, to offer a single connection point for facilitating money movement to multiple endpoints through various form factors and innovative technologies across more than 200 countries and territories. With the emergence of new forms of commerce and money movement, we believe Visa's trusted brand, global network, security capabilities and risk management expertise position us to serve as a trust layer across the ecosystem, helping clients and partners adopt new technologies and payment experiences with confidence. Visa is committed to advancing innovat","zh":null},{"en":"We offer a wide range of Visa-branded payment products that our clients, including over 14,000 financial institutions, use to develop and offer payment solutions or services, including credit, debit, prepaid and cash access programs for individual, business and government account holders. During fiscal 2026, Visa's total payments and cash volume was $18 trillion, and we had over 5 billion payment credentials, which are issued Visa card accounts, that were available to be used at more than 400 million(1) seller locations worldwide.","zh":null}],"markets":[],"customers":[{"en":"Even with our strong foundation in credit, significant opportunity remains in international markets, where the penetration of card-linked credit products as a percentage of consumer spending is less than half that of the U.S. To address this, we continue to develop products and capabilities that help issuers launch, manage and differentiate credit programs while providing greater flexibility, control and insight to our issuing clients and their customers. For example, Visa Flex Credential allows consumers to use a single Visa payment credential to access and switch","zh":null}],"competition":[{"en":"The global payments industry continues to undergo dynamic and rapid change. Existing and emerging competitors compete with Visa's network and payment solutions for consumers and for participation by financial institutions and sellers. Technology and innovation are shifting consumer habits and driving growth opportunities in ecommerce, GenAI agent-based commerce, mobile payments, blockchain technology and digital currencies, including stablecoins. These advances are enabling new entrants, many of which depart from traditional network payment models. In certain countries, the evolving regulatory landscape is creating local networks or enabling additional processing competition.","zh":null},{"en":"We compete against all forms of payment. These include paper-based payments, primarily cash and checks, and all forms of electronic payments. Our electronic payment competitors principally include the ones listed below.","zh":null}],"segments":{"prod":{"end":"2026-09-30","items":[{"name":"Data Processing Revenues","val":23374000000,"zh":"Data Processing Revenues"},{"name":"Service","val":19918000000,"zh":"服務"},{"name":"International Transaction Revenues","val":15251000000,"zh":"International Transaction Revenues"},{"name":"Value Added Services","val":14200000000,"zh":"Value Added Services"},{"name":"Service Other","val":5677000000,"zh":"Service Other"}],"total":45903000000},"geo":{"end":"2026-09-30","items":[{"name":"Non Us","val":28480000000,"zh":"Non Us"},{"name":"US","val":17423000000,"zh":"美國"}],"total":45903000000}},"peers":["MA","PYPL","AXP","COST","JPM"]}}